1
00:00:05,133 --> 00:00:12,100
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,767 --> 00:00:32,533
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:35,467
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:40,167 --> 00:00:41,300
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,167 --> 00:00:43,667
[ENGINE REVVING]

6
00:00:43,667 --> 00:00:45,533
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,533 --> 00:00:46,800
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:47,433 --> 00:00:48,800
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:51,567
- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]

10
00:00:52,333 --> 00:00:53,600
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:56,000
- [ENGINES REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,833 --> 00:00:58,633
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,633 --> 00:01:00,433
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:03,167
[ENGINE REVVING]

15
00:01:05,267 --> 00:01:06,567
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:09,300
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,133
- [GUNSHOT]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:12,133 --> 00:01:13,233
- [TRUCK HORN BLARES]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,233 --> 00:01:15,133
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:21,867
<i>The NCIA is having
an event today.</i>

21
00:01:21,867 --> 00:01:24,533
<i>If you want to bring
them down, come here.</i>

22
00:01:24,533 --> 00:01:27,333
<i>No one moves
unless I tell you to.</i>

23
00:01:27,333 --> 00:01:29,500
We'll move in exactly one hour.

24
00:01:29,500 --> 00:01:30,700
<i> One hour.</i>

25
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:31,667
<i> Good evening, Sir.</i>

26
00:01:31,667 --> 00:01:32,967
<i> Let's go here.</i>

27
00:01:32,967 --> 00:01:36,367
<i>Here in our place, you need
to be brave to survive.</i>

28
00:01:36,367 --> 00:01:38,700
<i>I've never met this
kind of man before.</i>

29
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:41,367
<i>Someone willing to risk
his life for other people.</i>

30
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:43,400
<i>I hope you don't
do that again.</i>

31
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:45,400
<i>I really trying
to turn my life around.</i>

32
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:48,400
<i>I promise that I'll turn
my life around.</i>

33
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,367
<i> For Gloria's sake.</i>

34
00:01:51,267 --> 00:01:53,567
[GRUNTS]

35
00:01:53,833 --> 00:01:55,400
This is so annoying!

36
00:01:56,267 --> 00:01:56,833
Hey.

37
00:01:57,833 --> 00:01:58,833
What?

38
00:01:58,833 --> 00:02:00,500
Have you come
to your senses yet?

39
00:02:00,567 --> 00:02:01,667
Have you realized
what you've done now?

40
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:04,900
You're right.

41
00:02:04,900 --> 00:02:07,467
Ricardo doesn't have
any influence anymore, right?

42
00:02:08,067 --> 00:02:09,367
What if later...

43
00:02:10,033 --> 00:02:11,900
his threats against me
might happen.

44
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:13,767
Finally! [LAUGHS]

45
00:02:13,800 --> 00:02:15,367
This is great!

46
00:02:15,567 --> 00:02:16,933
You've finally come
to your senses!

47
00:02:16,933 --> 00:02:18,433
Congratulations!

48
00:02:18,433 --> 00:02:19,767
- How could I not?
- What?

49
00:02:19,767 --> 00:02:22,400
[COUGHS] We can't miss
an episode, can we?

50
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:24,933
My fans are all waiting for me!

51
00:02:24,933 --> 00:02:26,567
Wait, wait, wait.

52
00:02:26,567 --> 00:02:29,067
You'll make an episode
with the boss' permission?

53
00:02:29,067 --> 00:02:30,533
- Yes.
- How?

54
00:02:30,533 --> 00:02:31,767
This is my show.

55
00:02:31,767 --> 00:02:34,600
I have the right to pick
which story to talk about.

56
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:35,967
And remember,

57
00:02:35,967 --> 00:02:39,567
my sympathetic face
and my good looks

58
00:02:39,567 --> 00:02:43,433
are what's at stake here,
not Ricardo's!

59
00:02:43,433 --> 00:02:48,000
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

60
00:02:49,767 --> 00:02:56,733
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

61
00:03:11,933 --> 00:03:18,933
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

62
00:03:33,933 --> 00:03:40,900
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

63
00:03:45,133 --> 00:03:47,133
[GABO] Love, are you alright?

64
00:03:47,133 --> 00:03:49,433
You may be tired.

65
00:03:50,667 --> 00:03:51,933
Me? Tired?

66
00:03:51,933 --> 00:03:53,367
You might be tired.

67
00:03:53,367 --> 00:03:56,667
Will you apply for another
job tomorrow, love?

68
00:03:56,700 --> 00:03:57,633
Yes.

69
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:02,700
I'm sorry if I
couldn't do it earlier.

70
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:05,933
Don't worry, I'll
do it tomorrow, I promise.

71
00:04:06,533 --> 00:04:07,700
I'll look for job applications.

72
00:04:07,900 --> 00:04:11,167
The clothes you'll wear
tomorrow are ready.

73
00:04:11,533 --> 00:04:12,733
I'll prepare it.

74
00:04:12,733 --> 00:04:13,867
I'll help you.

75
00:04:13,867 --> 00:04:15,867
I'll iron it so you won't
get tired.

76
00:04:16,200 --> 00:04:17,367
Okay.

77
00:04:18,533 --> 00:04:21,000
Auntie, we'll be at the room.

78
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:22,500
Gloria will just get
my clothes ready.

79
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:24,500
- Hmm. Okay.
- Okay.

80
00:04:24,867 --> 00:04:26,667
Hmm.

81
00:04:27,700 --> 00:04:28,700
[GABO] Oh, hey!

82
00:04:29,100 --> 00:04:30,433
Where did that come from?

83
00:04:30,433 --> 00:04:32,200
These are your options
for tomorrow.

84
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:33,867
Let's look through them
and have you try them on.

85
00:04:34,433 --> 00:04:35,733
This is a lot!
Where did it come from?

86
00:04:35,733 --> 00:04:37,000
We borrowed them.

87
00:04:38,167 --> 00:04:39,700
What about this?

88
00:04:39,700 --> 00:04:44,067
I think we could make this work,
but it looks too casual.

89
00:04:44,067 --> 00:04:45,433
Wait a minute.

90
00:04:45,433 --> 00:04:47,067
I saw one earlier...

91
00:04:47,067 --> 00:04:48,167
Here!

92
00:04:48,167 --> 00:04:51,000
You have to wear white to
look decent.

93
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,000
Oh, okay.

94
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:53,033
- Let me try.
- And...

95
00:04:53,567 --> 00:04:54,967
Here. Try it on.

96
00:04:55,233 --> 00:04:56,567
And this!

97
00:04:56,567 --> 00:04:58,667
Black pants would
look good with it.

98
00:04:58,667 --> 00:05:00,400
There's still a jacket here.
Try it on too.

99
00:05:01,700 --> 00:05:04,733
[CHUCKLES] Love,
this jacket looks good.

100
00:05:05,033 --> 00:05:06,933
I'd look like
a celebrity wearing this.

101
00:05:06,933 --> 00:05:08,567
That would look good
with this.

102
00:05:09,067 --> 00:05:09,833
Let me see.

103
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:11,667
You're right.

104
00:05:11,967 --> 00:05:13,533
Gabo, we have a problem.

105
00:05:13,933 --> 00:05:15,600
There's a hole.
What are we going to do?

106
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:17,867
It looks good with
the black pants.

107
00:05:17,867 --> 00:05:20,200
[CHUCKLES] Oh,
love, this is easy.

108
00:05:20,200 --> 00:05:21,867
I'll sew it up.
Give me a minute.

109
00:05:21,867 --> 00:05:23,933
I'll get a sewing kit
in Mama Betchay's room.

110
00:05:28,733 --> 00:05:35,733
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

111
00:05:50,767 --> 00:05:57,700
[INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES]

112
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,067
Here it is.

113
00:06:13,867 --> 00:06:14,933
Love!

114
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:17,800
Here it is, love.

115
00:06:18,200 --> 00:06:19,633
[GABO CHUCKLES]

116
00:06:19,633 --> 00:06:21,133
Here we go.

117
00:06:21,833 --> 00:06:24,300
Let's sew it up.
[CHUCKLES]

118
00:06:24,300 --> 00:06:25,933
- There a black thread.
- A black thread.

119
00:06:28,033 --> 00:06:32,633
Back when I was studying,
I was the best at sewing.

120
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:34,967
I was my teachers favorite.

121
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,667
[CHUCKLES]

122
00:06:37,667 --> 00:06:39,767
See? It's that simple.

123
00:06:39,767 --> 00:06:42,100
- How big is it?
- It's a bit big.

124
00:06:42,133 --> 00:06:43,667
Big? Don't worry.

125
00:06:43,667 --> 00:06:50,633
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

126
00:06:50,967 --> 00:06:51,833
Is it in?

127
00:06:52,367 --> 00:06:53,333
Wait.

128
00:06:56,800 --> 00:06:58,667
- It's not in.
- It's close.

129
00:07:01,367 --> 00:07:02,633
No.

130
00:07:02,633 --> 00:07:09,600
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

131
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:12,367
- Hey.
- I can't see it.

132
00:07:12,367 --> 00:07:13,833
The hole is small.

133
00:07:14,033 --> 00:07:15,167
Would you like to help me?

134
00:07:16,067 --> 00:07:18,000
- Can you?
- I'll try.

135
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:21,900
[BOTH CHUCKLING]

136
00:07:26,233 --> 00:07:27,233
Well?

137
00:07:27,233 --> 00:07:28,233
Can you?

138
00:07:28,233 --> 00:07:29,233
I got it in.

139
00:07:31,267 --> 00:07:34,000
Are you not yet sleepy?

140
00:07:34,067 --> 00:07:36,000
I'm still finishing this.

141
00:07:36,233 --> 00:07:37,200
Mameng.

142
00:07:38,067 --> 00:07:39,300
Where's Gabo and Gloria?

143
00:07:39,667 --> 00:07:41,233
They're in the room.

144
00:07:41,233 --> 00:07:46,900
Gloria is fixing Gabo's
clothes for tomorrow.

145
00:07:48,267 --> 00:07:49,267
You know what, Mameng,

146
00:07:49,867 --> 00:07:51,433
Gloria's kind, isn't she?

147
00:07:51,433 --> 00:07:53,200
She takes good care of Gabo.

148
00:07:53,733 --> 00:07:56,600
I hope they end up together.

149
00:07:56,933 --> 00:07:59,133
That is what we should
be praying for.

150
00:07:59,133 --> 00:08:02,200
Will we not call it
a night yet?

151
00:08:03,133 --> 00:08:03,933
[GROWL]

152
00:08:03,933 --> 00:08:06,767
Why are you growling?!

153
00:08:06,767 --> 00:08:08,133
- Goodnight, Rudy.
- Night.

154
00:08:08,133 --> 00:08:09,367
I'm so sleepy.

155
00:08:09,367 --> 00:08:11,100
[MAMENG] Quit it, Dante!

156
00:08:15,067 --> 00:08:17,033
<i> With all of this happening...</i>

157
00:08:18,367 --> 00:08:20,900
I hope my son doesn't get hurt.

158
00:08:20,900 --> 00:08:25,100
[MELANCHOLIC MUSIC PLAYING,
FADES]

159
00:08:26,833 --> 00:08:29,267
Put the end here...

160
00:08:30,133 --> 00:08:31,100
so it'll form a knot.

161
00:08:31,900 --> 00:08:32,867
See?

162
00:08:33,400 --> 00:08:37,100
You don't know how
to sew, do you?

163
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:41,133
Of course, your memory
hasn't come back yet.

164
00:08:42,100 --> 00:08:46,133
Earlier, I felt sorry for you

165
00:08:46,133 --> 00:08:47,800
because I knew

166
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:49,767
there were a lot of things
you couldn't remember.

167
00:08:50,133 --> 00:08:52,100
Like when we did
the laundry there.

168
00:08:53,100 --> 00:08:55,133
You barely even knew
how to do laundry.

169
00:08:55,167 --> 00:08:57,367
But you know,
when you were in jail,

170
00:08:57,367 --> 00:08:58,967
you were one of the
hardworking ones there

171
00:08:58,967 --> 00:09:00,333
who liked doing laundry.

172
00:09:00,333 --> 00:09:02,133
I was always waiting
for you there.

173
00:09:02,133 --> 00:09:03,100
[SAM SLIGHTLY LAUGHS]

174
00:09:03,100 --> 00:09:05,167
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

175
00:09:05,167 --> 00:09:06,133
You know, love,

176
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:07,967
thank you.

177
00:09:08,833 --> 00:09:09,833
For...

178
00:09:10,767 --> 00:09:13,133
giving me the time to

179
00:09:13,133 --> 00:09:16,133
help me
get our life back on track.

180
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:18,300
Honestly,

181
00:09:18,933 --> 00:09:20,767
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

182
00:09:20,767 --> 00:09:22,667
I'm a little nervous
about tomorrow.

183
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:27,267
Because I didn't finish
my studies.

184
00:09:27,300 --> 00:09:30,267
What if the people
I apply to

185
00:09:31,300 --> 00:09:32,900
look down on me?

186
00:09:32,900 --> 00:09:34,133
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

187
00:09:34,133 --> 00:09:35,100
Gabo.

188
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:37,200
You've already practiced.

189
00:09:38,367 --> 00:09:40,900
Besides,
that diploma

190
00:09:40,900 --> 00:09:42,167
is just a piece of paper.

191
00:09:42,167 --> 00:09:43,500
That's not what's important.

192
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:46,800
I hope you always remember
that you're smart.

193
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:48,167
More than anything,
you have a good heart.

194
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:50,900
You have determination.

195
00:09:50,900 --> 00:09:52,167
That's what's important.

196
00:09:53,133 --> 00:09:54,467
It's not about those papers.

197
00:09:54,467 --> 00:09:57,333
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

198
00:09:57,333 --> 00:09:58,433
But of course, love,

199
00:10:00,167 --> 00:10:02,267
even so,

200
00:10:02,367 --> 00:10:04,333
it's still different
when you finish your studies.

201
00:10:04,900 --> 00:10:07,167
When you finish your studies,

202
00:10:07,167 --> 00:10:08,367
you have something
to be proud of.

203
00:10:09,367 --> 00:10:11,333
You have something
to fall back on wherever you go.

204
00:10:12,433 --> 00:10:13,367
[GABO SIGHS]

205
00:10:13,900 --> 00:10:15,233
You know, back then,

206
00:10:15,233 --> 00:10:17,300
I used to feel sad whenever
I thought about my mother.

207
00:10:18,533 --> 00:10:20,233
Because when I was young,

208
00:10:21,233 --> 00:10:23,233
she was always the one
helping me with school.

209
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:25,500
That's why I regret it.

210
00:10:26,367 --> 00:10:28,000
Maybe if she were still alive,

211
00:10:29,400 --> 00:10:31,167
she would've guided me.

212
00:10:31,767 --> 00:10:33,867
Maybe I would've
finished school.

213
00:10:33,867 --> 00:10:37,267
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

214
00:10:37,300 --> 00:10:38,333
[GABO INHALES SOFTLY]

215
00:10:39,933 --> 00:10:41,367
That's why my dream

216
00:10:42,533 --> 00:10:44,267
and the promise I made to myself

217
00:10:45,300 --> 00:10:47,533
is that when I have a family
and children,

218
00:10:47,533 --> 00:10:48,900
I'll do everything

219
00:10:49,933 --> 00:10:52,233
to make sure
they finish their studies.

220
00:10:52,233 --> 00:10:53,533
Because I know

221
00:10:53,533 --> 00:10:55,800
that's the only thing
I can leave them

222
00:10:55,800 --> 00:10:57,600
that no one can take away.

223
00:10:57,600 --> 00:11:02,233
[MELLOW MUSIC CONTINUES]

224
00:11:02,233 --> 00:11:04,267
[GABO SLIGHTLY LAUGHS]

225
00:11:04,267 --> 00:11:05,267
I'm sorry.

226
00:11:05,267 --> 00:11:07,267
Sometimes, I really can't help

227
00:11:07,267 --> 00:11:08,867
but remember my mother.

228
00:11:10,567 --> 00:11:13,833
But Papa Rudy has never
let me down, either.

229
00:11:13,833 --> 00:11:15,433
That's why I'm telling you now

230
00:11:15,433 --> 00:11:18,267
how much you've helped me
by being in my life,

231
00:11:19,300 --> 00:11:20,433
guiding me

232
00:11:21,567 --> 00:11:23,267
and taking care
of my whole family.

233
00:11:26,333 --> 00:11:28,367
So thank you so, so much.

234
00:11:31,467 --> 00:11:32,467
[GABO SIGHS]

235
00:11:32,467 --> 00:11:34,233
Don't worry. Tomorrow,

236
00:11:35,067 --> 00:11:36,300
I promise you,

237
00:11:36,300 --> 00:11:38,233
- I won't come home
- [SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

238
00:11:38,233 --> 00:11:40,300
without getting a job.

239
00:11:40,300 --> 00:11:41,267
[GABO CHUCKLES]

240
00:11:41,633 --> 00:11:43,000
You can do it.

241
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:45,033
Since you taught me earlier

242
00:11:45,033 --> 00:11:47,133
how to apply for a job tomorrow,

243
00:11:47,133 --> 00:11:49,467
I'll teach you how to sew.

244
00:11:49,933 --> 00:11:51,300
- Okay.
- There.

245
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:53,300
[GABO] You need to line this up.

246
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,300
And then,

247
00:11:55,300 --> 00:11:56,967
you see the stitches?

248
00:11:56,967 --> 00:11:58,533
Since that's where
it got broken,

249
00:11:58,533 --> 00:12:01,133
that's where you'll sew it
so it won't be noticeable.

250
00:12:01,933 --> 00:12:03,000
There.

251
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,100
Once you get it through...

252
00:12:05,167 --> 00:12:07,533
<i>Whoever you marry
will be very lucky.</i>

253
00:12:07,533 --> 00:12:10,967
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

254
00:12:10,967 --> 00:12:12,233
<i> With your kind heart</i>

255
00:12:13,100 --> 00:12:14,133
<i> and your abilities,</i>

256
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:17,933
<i> any woman you'll truly love</i>

257
00:12:18,567 --> 00:12:20,567
<i> will surely be blessed.</i>

258
00:12:20,567 --> 00:12:27,500
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
BY GARY VALENCIANO PLAYING]

259
00:12:43,833 --> 00:12:45,467
- [SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]
- [GABO] See? It's fast.

260
00:12:46,067 --> 00:12:48,600
Because it's laid flat properly.

261
00:12:49,900 --> 00:12:50,900
It's almost done.

262
00:12:51,367 --> 00:12:53,067
See? There you go.

263
00:12:54,167 --> 00:12:55,367
Go ahead. You can hang it up.

264
00:12:57,233 --> 00:12:59,067
[GABO EXHALES SOFTLY]
Oh, love,

265
00:13:00,333 --> 00:13:01,900
I'm just going out
for a bit, okay?

266
00:13:02,100 --> 00:13:03,267
Okay.

267
00:13:03,267 --> 00:13:05,233
I'll finish that.
I'll take care of it.

268
00:13:05,233 --> 00:13:06,800
- [SOFT THUD]
- I'll just turn it off

269
00:13:07,733 --> 00:13:08,667
- [SOFT THUD]
- so you don't get burned.

270
00:13:10,367 --> 00:13:17,333
- [SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [FOOTSTEPS RECEDING]

271
00:13:20,933 --> 00:13:22,367
<i> I feel sorry for Gloria</i>

272
00:13:23,900 --> 00:13:26,300
<i>because I know she grew up
with a different kind of life.</i>

273
00:13:26,300 --> 00:13:28,133
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
INSTRUMENTAL PLAYING]

274
00:13:28,133 --> 00:13:30,100
But this is the only way I know

275
00:13:31,267 --> 00:13:33,167
<i> to protect her.</i>

276
00:13:37,767 --> 00:13:39,167
<i> I need to do something.</i>

277
00:13:40,300 --> 00:13:42,933
<i> I need to earn a lot of money</i>

278
00:13:42,933 --> 00:13:45,400
<i>so I can give her a good
and comfortable life.</i>

279
00:13:46,467 --> 00:13:47,400
<i> I hope...</i>

280
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:49,933
<i> now that we're together,</i>

281
00:13:50,967 --> 00:13:52,433
<i> I can make her happy.</i>

282
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:57,167
<i>If this is all just a dream
for the two of us,</i>

283
00:13:58,500 --> 00:14:00,433
<i> I don't ever want to wake up.</i>

284
00:14:02,100 --> 00:14:05,133
<i>I don't think I could bear
losing Gloria from my life.</i>

285
00:14:05,133 --> 00:14:12,033
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
INSTRUMENTAL CONTINUES]

286
00:14:26,433 --> 00:14:33,400
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
INSTRUMENTAL CONTINUES]

287
00:14:34,333 --> 00:14:35,833
[PRIEST] Tonight,

288
00:14:35,833 --> 00:14:38,167
we gather to remember
the life of Samantha Jacinto.

289
00:14:39,033 --> 00:14:41,400
- [MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- In the lives of those we love,

290
00:14:42,133 --> 00:14:45,100
there are memories
that never fade.

291
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:47,900
Samantha Jacinto.

292
00:14:49,133 --> 00:14:50,467
What an amazing woman.

293
00:14:52,333 --> 00:14:53,500
Very hardworking.

294
00:14:53,967 --> 00:14:54,933
Very kind.

295
00:14:56,267 --> 00:14:57,233
Ma'am Sam.

296
00:14:59,167 --> 00:15:01,167
She may have been
a woman, but...

297
00:15:01,900 --> 00:15:03,500
she was always the first
to charge in.

298
00:15:04,367 --> 00:15:06,300
The first to face danger.

299
00:15:06,633 --> 00:15:08,867
That's why I truly admired
her courage.

300
00:15:09,033 --> 00:15:11,000
She was the one who...

301
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:13,300
always reminded us that

302
00:15:13,300 --> 00:15:15,167
before any mission,

303
00:15:15,167 --> 00:15:18,133
what mattered more
was our bond with each another.

304
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:20,167
You know, with Ma'am Sam,

305
00:15:20,967 --> 00:15:24,867
we never once treated each other
as mere coworkers.

306
00:15:24,867 --> 00:15:27,667
Because Ma'am Sam
was like a younger sister to me.

307
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:30,100
Hi, Sam.

308
00:15:31,033 --> 00:15:33,000
My best friend forever.

309
00:15:33,200 --> 00:15:35,167
No matter how difficult
the mission was,

310
00:15:35,900 --> 00:15:37,233
she made it easy.

311
00:15:39,067 --> 00:15:42,167
Because she always reminded us
to help each other.

312
00:15:42,900 --> 00:15:45,900
It's such a shame
you left us so soon.

313
00:15:45,900 --> 00:15:49,100
We could have been
happy together.

314
00:15:49,100 --> 00:15:51,367
I never even got to show you

315
00:15:53,933 --> 00:15:57,867
how to be
the best boyfriend ever.

316
00:16:00,400 --> 00:16:01,700
We will miss you.

317
00:16:02,700 --> 00:16:03,767
We love you.

318
00:16:03,767 --> 00:16:05,400
Wherever you are now,

319
00:16:05,400 --> 00:16:07,933
thank you so, so much
for everything we shared.

320
00:16:07,933 --> 00:16:09,167
We love you, Ma'am Sam.

321
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:10,767
Until we meet again.

322
00:16:10,767 --> 00:16:17,733
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

323
00:16:19,100 --> 00:16:25,100
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [CLOCK TICKING]

324
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:26,100
Is anyone else coming?

325
00:16:26,100 --> 00:16:27,167
[TENSE STING]

326
00:16:28,267 --> 00:16:30,200
Uh-- [SCOFFS]
No.

327
00:16:30,367 --> 00:16:31,400
No one else, sir.

328
00:16:31,400 --> 00:16:38,367
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

329
00:16:38,633 --> 00:16:40,400
[LUCAS] What? Has it been
an hour already?

330
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:42,067
[ARTURO] 10 more minutes.

331
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:47,067
Lucas, we'll go inside instead.

332
00:16:47,067 --> 00:16:48,133
No.

333
00:16:48,133 --> 00:16:49,367
This is my mission.

334
00:16:50,667 --> 00:16:51,900
You're a Zafra.

335
00:16:52,233 --> 00:16:53,833
They might recognize you.
It'll be more dangerous

336
00:16:53,833 --> 00:16:55,400
if you get caught too.

337
00:16:55,400 --> 00:16:56,867
We'll finish the mission.

338
00:16:58,800 --> 00:17:00,133
Who gave you that order?

339
00:17:01,167 --> 00:17:02,133
From Papa?

340
00:17:02,733 --> 00:17:04,100
Why would I follow you?

341
00:17:04,733 --> 00:17:06,133
You're just here to take orders.

342
00:17:06,133 --> 00:17:07,400
You're the one
who should follow me.

343
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:08,400
[TENSE STING]

344
00:17:11,267 --> 00:17:12,700
[TENSE STING]

345
00:17:12,767 --> 00:17:14,133
- Sir, I'll go ahead.
- [DELGADO] Hold on, Pia.

346
00:17:14,133 --> 00:17:16,933
Sit down. I have, uh,
an announcement to make.

347
00:17:18,333 --> 00:17:19,333
Excuse me.

348
00:17:19,333 --> 00:17:21,967
I have an announcement to make.

349
00:17:22,933 --> 00:17:24,233
Team.

350
00:17:24,300 --> 00:17:28,467
A lot has happened in our agency
over the past few weeks.

351
00:17:29,133 --> 00:17:31,833
We've lost many, including Sam.

352
00:17:31,833 --> 00:17:35,133
But we've also accomplished
many missions.

353
00:17:35,133 --> 00:17:37,967
We've defeated many
of our enemies.

354
00:17:38,333 --> 00:17:41,100
One of them was Victor Zafra.

355
00:17:41,100 --> 00:17:46,267
A high-profile syndicate leader
we apprehended,

356
00:17:46,267 --> 00:17:49,933
who is now detained
in a maximum-security facility.

357
00:17:49,967 --> 00:17:53,200
And this was all possible...

358
00:17:53,200 --> 00:17:54,733
because of Sam.

359
00:17:54,733 --> 00:17:59,367
[APPLAUSE]

360
00:17:59,367 --> 00:18:01,200
But the fight isn't over yet.

361
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:03,200
Which is why
I gathered you here tonight

362
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:06,200
to honor Sam's memory.

363
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:10,800
At the same time,
I want to honor you all

364
00:18:10,800 --> 00:18:12,200
for a job well done.

365
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:13,367
To Sam!

366
00:18:13,367 --> 00:18:14,300
[IN UNISON]
To Sam!

367
00:18:14,300 --> 00:18:15,300
To Sam!

368
00:18:15,300 --> 00:18:16,367
[IN UNISON]
To Sam!

369
00:18:16,367 --> 00:18:17,233
To Sam!

370
00:18:17,233 --> 00:18:18,367
[IN UNISON]
To Sam!

371
00:18:18,367 --> 00:18:22,000
Lao, tell our people
to get ready.

372
00:18:22,033 --> 00:18:23,067
We're going in.

373
00:18:23,067 --> 00:18:25,033
Boys, get in position.

374
00:18:25,033 --> 00:18:29,167
[APPLAUSE]

375
00:18:30,567 --> 00:18:32,933
And the best way
to honor Sam

376
00:18:32,933 --> 00:18:35,100
is to continue
her work and legacy.

377
00:18:35,100 --> 00:18:38,000
So tonight, we're going to
find the rightful person

378
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,233
to take her place
as team leader.

379
00:18:40,233 --> 00:18:41,400
[SEBASTIAN CLEARS THROAT]

380
00:18:41,400 --> 00:18:44,500
To continue the fight
against the Zafras,

381
00:18:44,500 --> 00:18:46,933
and finish the cases
she left behind.

382
00:18:46,933 --> 00:18:49,500
Sir, we all know that

383
00:18:49,500 --> 00:18:51,367
Sebastian deserves
that position the most.

384
00:18:51,367 --> 00:18:53,833
- She's right, Sebastian!
- [SEBASTIAN HUFFS]

385
00:18:53,833 --> 00:18:54,933
Really, sir?

386
00:18:54,967 --> 00:18:57,867
You have been chosen
as the new team leader

387
00:18:57,867 --> 00:19:01,100
who will continue
what Sam started.

388
00:19:01,100 --> 00:19:02,067
Congratulations!

389
00:19:02,067 --> 00:19:03,100
Thank you, sir.

390
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:05,433
[APPLAUSE]

391
00:19:05,433 --> 00:19:06,900
[CHUCKLES]

392
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:09,933
- Cheers!
- [BOTTLES CLINK]

393
00:19:09,933 --> 00:19:11,367
[CHUCKLES]

394
00:19:11,367 --> 00:19:13,033
- Hmm?
- Seb.

395
00:19:13,033 --> 00:19:14,100
Come with me.

396
00:19:14,100 --> 00:19:16,100
Let's celebrate your promotion.

397
00:19:16,100 --> 00:19:17,267
Where are we going?

398
00:19:17,267 --> 00:19:18,400
Anywhere you want.
Come on, let's go.

399
00:19:18,400 --> 00:19:20,433
No, no, no.
I need to give a speech.

400
00:19:20,433 --> 00:19:23,867
Then I want to celebrate
with my team.

401
00:19:23,867 --> 00:19:26,267
I'm going to give my speech.
I'll be right back.

402
00:19:26,267 --> 00:19:27,933
- Sir.
- [APPLAUSE]

403
00:19:27,933 --> 00:19:29,067
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

404
00:19:29,100 --> 00:19:30,267
- Congratulations.
- Thank you, thank you.

405
00:19:30,267 --> 00:19:32,000
- [SEBASTIAN CHUCKLES]
- Congratulations.

406
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,433
- I told you guys!
- Mm.

407
00:19:34,433 --> 00:19:36,267
Thank you so much, everyone.

408
00:19:36,267 --> 00:19:42,067
I know that
Sam is really proud of me.

409
00:19:42,067 --> 00:19:45,967
[GUNS COCKING, CLICKING]

410
00:19:45,967 --> 00:19:50,433
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

411
00:19:51,967 --> 00:19:53,700
First of all,
thank you very much.

412
00:19:54,333 --> 00:20:00,767
I know that Sam
is really proud of me.

413
00:20:00,833 --> 00:20:03,100
And I know exactly
what she's thinking.

414
00:20:03,133 --> 00:20:06,100
I am the best choice

415
00:20:06,100 --> 00:20:09,600
to continue what she started.

416
00:20:09,600 --> 00:20:13,967
It's just unfortunate that
Sam won't get to see

417
00:20:13,967 --> 00:20:15,967
the result of her hard work.

418
00:20:15,967 --> 00:20:17,933
[CLOCK TICKING]

419
00:20:17,933 --> 00:20:19,300
[LUCAS] Lao, step on it.

420
00:20:19,300 --> 00:20:20,633
[ARTURO] Wait,
there's five minutes left.

421
00:20:20,633 --> 00:20:21,967
That doesn't matter!

422
00:20:21,967 --> 00:20:23,133
Come on! Let's attack!

423
00:20:23,133 --> 00:20:24,367
[ENGINE REVS]

424
00:20:24,367 --> 00:20:25,567
[TIRES SCREECH]

425
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:31,300
To Sam, I'll make you proud.

426
00:20:32,333 --> 00:20:33,933
As for the Zafras,

427
00:20:33,933 --> 00:20:36,033
I will do everything in my power

428
00:20:36,067 --> 00:20:40,067
to make sure they pay
for what they did to you.

429
00:20:40,067 --> 00:20:42,233
- [CLOCK TICKING]
- [SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

430
00:20:42,233 --> 00:20:43,267
[GRUNTS]

431
00:20:45,633 --> 00:20:50,000
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

432
00:20:50,000 --> 00:20:51,300
So Sam, this is for you.

433
00:20:51,300 --> 00:20:52,333
For Sam!

434
00:20:52,333 --> 00:20:57,500
[IN UNISON]
For Sam!

435
00:20:57,500 --> 00:21:03,333
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

436
00:21:03,333 --> 00:21:05,667
- [LUCAS SHOUTING]
- [RAPID GUNFIRE]

437
00:21:05,667 --> 00:21:09,667
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

438
00:21:09,700 --> 00:21:11,167
Get down!

439
00:21:11,167 --> 00:21:15,600
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

440
00:21:15,600 --> 00:21:22,633
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

441
00:21:27,500 --> 00:21:29,400
[OBJECTS CLATTER]

442
00:21:29,400 --> 00:21:33,100
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

443
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:34,100
[HUFFS]

444
00:21:34,100 --> 00:21:41,000
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

445
00:21:44,033 --> 00:21:46,300
[GUNSHOTS]

446
00:21:46,300 --> 00:21:53,333
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

447
00:21:54,433 --> 00:21:56,433
Enough! Mission accomplished!
Let's go, Lucas!

448
00:21:56,433 --> 00:22:00,133
[RAPID GUNFIRE CONTINUES]

449
00:22:00,133 --> 00:22:01,567
[LUCAS SHOUTING]

450
00:22:01,567 --> 00:22:03,733
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

451
00:22:03,733 --> 00:22:04,733
[ARTURO] Enough!

452
00:22:04,733 --> 00:22:08,400
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

453
00:22:08,400 --> 00:22:10,033
Go after them!

454
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:13,533
[FRAME CLATTERS]

455
00:22:13,533 --> 00:22:20,433
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

456
00:22:22,433 --> 00:22:23,633
[GRUNTS WEAKLY]

457
00:22:25,600 --> 00:22:27,233
[TIRES SCREECH]

458
00:22:29,233 --> 00:22:30,433
[GUNSHOTS]

459
00:22:30,433 --> 00:22:31,467
[SEBASTIAN GRUNTS]

460
00:22:31,467 --> 00:22:32,600
[GUNSHOTS]

461
00:22:32,600 --> 00:22:33,633
Aah!

462
00:22:33,633 --> 00:22:35,100
[GUNSHOTS]

463
00:22:36,300 --> 00:22:42,267
[RAPID GUNFIRE]

464
00:22:42,267 --> 00:22:44,400
We need to go back
for Sir Delgado!

465
00:22:44,400 --> 00:22:46,167
- Come on!
- Sir Delgado!

466
00:22:46,167 --> 00:22:48,067
- Come on!
- Let's go!

467
00:22:49,633 --> 00:22:51,133
Sir!

468
00:22:51,133 --> 00:22:52,700
- Sir?
- Sir!

469
00:22:52,700 --> 00:22:54,600
- Sir!
- Sir!

470
00:22:54,600 --> 00:22:56,000
Sir!

471
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,633
Sir... He's hit.

472
00:22:58,467 --> 00:23:00,100
- Oh, no.
- He's hit.

473
00:23:00,100 --> 00:23:01,467
Did anyone else get hit?

474
00:23:01,467 --> 00:23:04,300
- There are a lot of casualties.
- [GROANS IN PAIN]

475
00:23:04,300 --> 00:23:05,767
[GRUNTING]

476
00:23:05,767 --> 00:23:07,800
Did you catch them?

477
00:23:07,800 --> 00:23:09,000
No, sir.

478
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:11,000
We couldn't catch up;
they escaped.

479
00:23:14,367 --> 00:23:15,667
[BREATH QUIVERING]

480
00:23:18,633 --> 00:23:20,500
[LAUGHING HYSTERICALLY]

481
00:23:20,500 --> 00:23:22,300
Sir, don't worry about that.

482
00:23:22,333 --> 00:23:23,800
We need to take
you to the hospital.

483
00:23:23,800 --> 00:23:25,633
- [DELGADO GRUNTS]
- Can you stand up?

484
00:23:25,633 --> 00:23:27,667
Borromeo!
Call an ambulance!

485
00:23:29,167 --> 00:23:31,067
Bullet!
Check for survivors!

486
00:23:31,067 --> 00:23:32,633
Copy.

487
00:23:32,633 --> 00:23:35,233
[DELGADO BREATHING LABORIOUSLY]

488
00:23:35,233 --> 00:23:39,367
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

489
00:23:39,367 --> 00:23:41,200
[BREATHES HEAVILY]

490
00:23:49,133 --> 00:23:50,100
Gabo.

491
00:23:51,333 --> 00:23:52,300
Hey.

492
00:23:53,333 --> 00:23:55,000
Why'd you follow me here?

493
00:23:55,700 --> 00:23:57,067
Are you okay?

494
00:23:59,067 --> 00:24:00,367
I'm fine.

495
00:24:00,367 --> 00:24:01,733
Just getting some air.

496
00:24:02,700 --> 00:24:05,067
It looks like
you're lost in your thoughts.

497
00:24:05,667 --> 00:24:11,333
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

498
00:24:11,333 --> 00:24:15,400
I was just thinking about
what happened earlier.

499
00:24:15,400 --> 00:24:19,367
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

500
00:24:19,367 --> 00:24:23,800
Even though
I don't remember everything yet,

501
00:24:25,767 --> 00:24:27,333
I admire you.

502
00:24:29,400 --> 00:24:33,533
You were willing to risk
your life for this community.

503
00:24:37,800 --> 00:24:39,233
[GABO EXHALES]

504
00:24:39,233 --> 00:24:40,767
You know what?

505
00:24:42,767 --> 00:24:44,733
I'd risk my life,
not only for my community,

506
00:24:46,533 --> 00:24:50,167
but for anyone in need.

507
00:24:51,800 --> 00:24:53,700
Especially you, Gloria.

508
00:24:56,733 --> 00:24:59,233
Just be careful, Gabo.

509
00:24:59,233 --> 00:25:02,467
There are a lot of people
who care about and love you.

510
00:25:02,500 --> 00:25:04,767
Especially your family.

511
00:25:04,767 --> 00:25:11,333
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

512
00:25:11,333 --> 00:25:12,933
I know that.

513
00:25:12,933 --> 00:25:18,433
But when I hear their call,

514
00:25:18,433 --> 00:25:22,633
I can't ignore those
who need my help.

515
00:25:24,267 --> 00:25:26,667
Especially those
who are oppressed.

516
00:25:26,667 --> 00:25:33,567
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

517
00:25:33,567 --> 00:25:38,133
Gloria, I'm willing to
lay down my life for you.

518
00:25:38,967 --> 00:25:41,167
I'd rather die

519
00:25:42,933 --> 00:25:45,167
than see you get hurt.

520
00:25:46,300 --> 00:25:48,267
I will always be
by your side.

521
00:25:49,200 --> 00:25:51,633
I will always protect
and take care of you.

522
00:25:51,633 --> 00:25:53,200
That's how much I love you.

523
00:25:53,200 --> 00:26:00,233
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
BY GARY VALENCIANO PLAYING]

524
00:26:14,567 --> 00:26:16,500
["KUNG KAILANGAN MO AKO"
CONTINUES]

525
00:26:19,867 --> 00:26:20,800
Ah...

526
00:26:21,333 --> 00:26:22,333
Let's sleep.

527
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:25,967
Come on.

528
00:26:25,967 --> 00:26:30,167
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

529
00:26:30,333 --> 00:26:32,100
I had my moment.

530
00:26:33,067 --> 00:26:34,433
Then it fell through.

531
00:26:36,467 --> 00:26:37,833
I was so close.

532
00:26:38,467 --> 00:26:45,433
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

533
00:26:53,600 --> 00:26:55,967
No one even checked on me!

534
00:26:56,533 --> 00:26:58,333
I was so scared!

535
00:26:58,333 --> 00:27:00,833
Not one of you
even checked on me!

536
00:27:01,167 --> 00:27:02,167
We're so sorry.

537
00:27:02,167 --> 00:27:04,000
Ma'am Pia, how are you?

538
00:27:04,933 --> 00:27:06,333
Sir, sir.
What do you think?

539
00:27:06,333 --> 00:27:08,500
Was this a random shoot, or
were we specifically targeted?

540
00:27:08,500 --> 00:27:10,300
We were targeted!

541
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:12,233
The Zafras!

542
00:27:12,233 --> 00:27:14,300
The Zafras are behind this!

543
00:27:14,667 --> 00:27:16,200
This has to stop.

544
00:27:16,233 --> 00:27:19,033
We can't lose anyone else
because of the Zafras!

545
00:27:19,700 --> 00:27:23,133
The Zafras will pay for what
they did to the NCIA.

546
00:27:23,133 --> 00:27:30,167
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

547
00:27:31,033 --> 00:27:33,400
Gabo, are you sure
Mama Betchay won't get mad?

548
00:27:33,400 --> 00:27:35,067
You're messing with her drink.

549
00:27:35,067 --> 00:27:36,067
That's fine.

550
00:27:36,700 --> 00:27:38,433
I'll just replace it tomorrow.

551
00:27:39,467 --> 00:27:41,600
Why did you suddenly
ask me to drink?

552
00:27:41,600 --> 00:27:43,233
To celebrate, of course.

553
00:27:43,233 --> 00:27:45,200
Because I'm sure I'll get
a job tomorrow.

554
00:27:45,200 --> 00:27:47,033
- [LAUGHS]
- [ICE CRACKING]

555
00:27:47,033 --> 00:27:49,333
Celebrate? You haven't
even applied yet.

556
00:27:50,467 --> 00:27:51,567
[CHUCKLES SLIGHTLY]

557
00:27:51,567 --> 00:27:54,333
Even though
I haven't applied yet,

558
00:27:54,333 --> 00:27:56,233
I'm sure tomorrow,

559
00:27:56,233 --> 00:27:58,533
different companies
will be fighting over me.

560
00:27:59,100 --> 00:28:00,900
I already know
how this will turn out.

561
00:28:02,267 --> 00:28:03,267
[CHUCKLES]

562
00:28:03,267 --> 00:28:06,167
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

563
00:28:06,167 --> 00:28:09,600
Let me ask you,
don't you have any vices?

564
00:28:10,167 --> 00:28:11,200
Vices?

565
00:28:12,067 --> 00:28:13,267
Uh...

566
00:28:13,267 --> 00:28:15,433
I drink occasionally,
when there's an occasion.

567
00:28:15,433 --> 00:28:16,633
But...

568
00:28:18,267 --> 00:28:19,700
...I really only have one vice.

569
00:28:20,433 --> 00:28:21,633
Do you know what it is?

570
00:28:21,633 --> 00:28:23,067
- What?
- [CHUCKLES]

571
00:28:23,100 --> 00:28:25,533
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

572
00:28:25,533 --> 00:28:28,400
To love and take care of you.

573
00:28:29,367 --> 00:28:30,967
[LAUGHS]

574
00:28:30,967 --> 00:28:32,267
You're not even drunk yet, huh?

575
00:28:32,267 --> 00:28:33,667
You're such a smooth talker.

576
00:28:36,433 --> 00:28:38,533
You probably had a lot
of girlfriends before, huh?

577
00:28:38,533 --> 00:28:41,400
I've never had a girlfriend,
not even when I was young.

578
00:28:42,267 --> 00:28:44,100
None? Not even one?

579
00:28:44,100 --> 00:28:45,100
None.

580
00:28:45,100 --> 00:28:46,467
Even though a lot of girls
liked me,

581
00:28:46,467 --> 00:28:47,600
I never paid attention to them.

582
00:28:48,200 --> 00:28:50,733
What about Tekla?

583
00:28:51,333 --> 00:28:53,700
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

584
00:28:53,700 --> 00:28:54,733
Tekla?

585
00:28:55,300 --> 00:28:56,767
She's just my childhood friend.

586
00:28:57,233 --> 00:28:59,700
And even when we were little,

587
00:28:59,700 --> 00:29:01,033
we were already friends,

588
00:29:01,633 --> 00:29:04,000
but that's really all it was.

589
00:29:05,233 --> 00:29:07,200
"Childhood friend," huh?

590
00:29:07,200 --> 00:29:09,433
It's so obvious
she's crazy about you.

591
00:29:11,467 --> 00:29:16,300
I'm not denying that Tekla
really likes me,

592
00:29:17,033 --> 00:29:18,467
but just because she likes me,

593
00:29:18,467 --> 00:29:20,333
that doesn't mean
I have to like her back.

594
00:29:20,800 --> 00:29:24,300
Of course,
my heart will decide

595
00:29:24,300 --> 00:29:25,967
who I will love.

596
00:29:27,133 --> 00:29:28,167
And that's you.

597
00:29:28,700 --> 00:29:30,367
[CHUCKLES SLIGHTY]

598
00:29:30,433 --> 00:29:34,533
I was just thinking,
why did I marry you?

599
00:29:36,500 --> 00:29:37,667
I don't know either.

600
00:29:38,200 --> 00:29:39,700
I was just surprised

601
00:29:39,700 --> 00:29:45,167
when you told me
that you liked me too.

602
00:29:46,767 --> 00:29:50,700
Maybe because I'm just simple.

603
00:29:51,767 --> 00:29:53,300
I stay true to myself.

604
00:29:54,700 --> 00:29:57,067
I don't really have anything
else to be proud of

605
00:29:57,067 --> 00:29:58,433
except for being myself.

606
00:29:58,433 --> 00:30:04,700
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

607
00:30:04,733 --> 00:30:06,200
You know,

608
00:30:06,200 --> 00:30:08,833
even though my memories
haven't come back yet,

609
00:30:09,700 --> 00:30:11,767
all I know is that
you're a good person.

610
00:30:14,367 --> 00:30:17,267
That's one thing
I'm absolutely sure of.

611
00:30:21,300 --> 00:30:22,567
You know, Gloria,

612
00:30:23,300 --> 00:30:25,067
there's something
I want to confess to you.

613
00:30:26,533 --> 00:30:30,433
Because whoever
you see me as right now,

614
00:30:31,567 --> 00:30:32,700
that's not the real me.

615
00:30:32,700 --> 00:30:38,300
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

616
00:30:38,333 --> 00:30:40,133
Do you know
why I asked you to drink?

617
00:30:45,100 --> 00:30:46,633
Because there's something
I want to confess to you.

618
00:30:49,467 --> 00:30:50,433
What is it?

619
00:30:54,500 --> 00:31:01,533
They say when there's alcohol,
there's a hidden agenda.

620
00:31:02,167 --> 00:31:03,400
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

621
00:31:03,400 --> 00:31:04,367
Hmm.

622
00:31:04,667 --> 00:31:06,567
- [LAUGHS AWKWARDLY]
- So...

623
00:31:08,600 --> 00:31:10,800
Maybe...

624
00:31:10,933 --> 00:31:16,133
Once we've finished this,
we can celebrate...

625
00:31:17,133 --> 00:31:19,233
me getting a job tomorrow.

626
00:31:19,533 --> 00:31:22,400
You're really sure you're going
to get a job, huh? [CHUCKLES]

627
00:31:24,133 --> 00:31:25,267
Cheers!

628
00:31:25,267 --> 00:31:26,333
- Hmm.
- [GLASSES CLINK]

629
00:31:26,333 --> 00:31:32,167
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

630
00:31:32,167 --> 00:31:33,500
[CHUCKLES AWKWARDLY]

631
00:31:34,533 --> 00:31:35,800
I'm a lion.

632
00:31:35,800 --> 00:31:38,267
[GROWLS]

633
00:31:43,533 --> 00:31:45,967
<i> - I almost died!
</i>- [SLAPS]

634
00:31:45,967 --> 00:31:49,133
<i>You know no one is getting
out of here alive, right?</i>

635
00:31:49,133 --> 00:31:53,033
<i>You can't imagine what pain
I'm going through right now.</i>

636
00:31:53,033 --> 00:31:57,900
<i>As a mother, I shouldn't be
mourning for my children.</i>

637
00:31:57,900 --> 00:32:01,467
I feel like I'm falling in love
<i> with you.</i>

638
00:32:01,467 --> 00:32:03,667
<i> Once you find out the truth,</i>

639
00:32:03,667 --> 00:32:05,067
<i> you'll leave me too.</i>

640
00:32:05,067 --> 00:32:09,133
<i>Gloria, I love you.
I really love you.</i>
